-- Endless Map - dungeon pages drawn from the client's OWN MINIMAP textures (+ the Deeprun Tram), and the
-- world-map doors of Forever's instances. GENERATED by tools/dungeonmapsmm/unify28.py from the verified research data
-- (tram, mapsA, mapsB, verify_inventory; no new measurements). fileDataIDs present locally (enUS) in 1.60.1.70058.
-- Load order: after DungeonMaps.lua (TOC). Entries here REPLACE ns.DUNGEON_MAPS[369] (the tram) or add new ids; NONE of
-- these ids is a uiMap: never pass anything from here to WorldMapFrame:SetMapID.
--
-- Floor fields beyond DungeonMaps.lua's n / g / r / t / s (a floor has exactly one of t, q, rq):
--   q   = quads { fileDataID, u0, v0, u1, v1, ULx, ULy, LLx, LLy, URx, URy, LRx, LRy, sublevel }: box on the 1002x668
--         picture (0..1, clipped to it), tex:SetTexCoord(the 8 values, all inside 0..1), ARTWORK sublevel
--   rq  = angled blocks { fileDataID, cx, cy, w, h, radians, sublevel }: the whole texture as a w x h quad centred on
--         picture px (cx, cy), turned by Texture:SetRotation(radians) about its centre (counter-clockwise), drawn in a
--         frame that clips to the picture (DungeonQuads.lua)
--   k   = the kind of minimap page (look: LOOK below): "terrain" | "building" | "line"
--   bgc = { r, g, b }: plain backdrop colour (letterboxed pages, when the look has no backdrop of its own)
--   ov  = overview floor: holds the whole map; picked from the position only where no other floor holds the player
--         (enter 2% inside another floor's picture, leave 1% past its edge); never fades dots, never vetoes the arrow
--   sz  = picked only by sub-zone name (s) or from the dropdown, never from the position
--   lv  = the ground a floor shows: floors with the same lv are crops of ONE level (City of Dalaran's city and the
--         Hillsbrad ground south of it), so a point on both is on both - its dot is not faded, the arrow not hidden
--   ar  = AreaTable ID whose C_Map.GetAreaInfo name is the floor name (localized); en = enUS dungeon name fallback
--   keep = (map) Blizzard's own automatic map changes - to exactly MapUtil.GetDisplayableMapForPlayer(): the player's
--         map, else its first parent with art (review) - leave the dungeon view open while the player is inside: these
--         instances have Eastern Kingdoms as cosmetic parent (D8)
--   cp  = (map) Map.db2 CosmeticParentMapID, set only where the instance is a copy of that continent at UNCHANGED world
--         coordinates (the engine research: every ADT tile best-matches map 0's tile of the same index): the group
--         widget (DungeonMarkers.lua) lays that continent's zone map onto the pages - the engine draws the player /
--         party there if it puts the instance on its parent's maps (in-game test), else nothing
-- Not here: Manor Mistmantle (Map.db2 3109) - its WDT (fileDataID 7937200) is not in the client (70009, 70058): no
-- tiles, no minimap, so no page. Re-check after the next client patch (D7).

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Switches (data only; each one is independent)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
